[summary: "Recursive" application of simple rules, such as in Conway's
Game of Life give rise to complex behavior. Recursive application of
the physical laws of the universe has given rise to the complex we
see today.]

> >>      Perhaps these recursive movements are are too complex for
> >> science, but we can ask, are these recursive patterns which have
> >> created the world and us, the hand of God?  Shall we endow the cold
> >> dead matter of universe with the power to arrange itself into
> >> concsious rational beings and create an environment that just
> >> happens to be suitable for us?  Or might we say that the
> >> recursively created patterns just may have been consciously
> >> designed.

    The author can answer this himself. Since recursive application
of these rules is what is responsible for the universe as we see
today, there is no place for God in the equation except as the creator
of the physical laws themselves. Asking whether the deterministically
created order we see is "the hand of God" is like asking whether
the "invisible hand of the free market" is a mystical god of finance
directing outcomes to his liking.

-Ray


